1
00:00:13,019 --> 00:00:16,170
♪ Hark! The Herald Angels sing

2
00:00:16,219 --> 00:00:19,449
♪ "Glory to the newborn king!"

3
00:00:19,500 --> 00:00:22,649
♪ Peace on earth and mercy mild

4
00:00:22,699 --> 00:00:26,050
♪ God and sinners reconciled

5
00:00:26,100 --> 00:00:29,329
♪ Joyful, all ye nations, rise

6
00:00:29,379 --> 00:00:32,700
♪ Join the triumph of the skies... ♪

7
00:00:42,060 --> 00:00:43,899
Nothing there.

8
00:00:47,219 --> 00:00:48,740
Oh!

9
00:00:50,539 --> 00:00:52,280
This must be it.

10
00:00:59,740 --> 00:01:01,090
Is there anything on my head?

11
00:01:01,140 --> 00:01:03,689
- Er, well, yes.
- Describe it.

12
00:01:03,740 --> 00:01:05,569
Well, you've sort of got antlers.

13
00:01:05,620 --> 00:01:07,930
- Antlers?
- Yes, antlers.

14
00:01:07,980 --> 00:01:09,719
- Antlers!
- Hm.

15
00:01:11,340 --> 00:01:13,530
You are a time-space machine!

16
00:01:13,579 --> 00:01:14,930
You're a vehicle!

17
00:01:14,980 --> 00:01:18,500
I've never asked you to cheer me
up with hologrammatic antlers!

18
00:01:19,539 --> 00:01:21,010
Thank you.

19
00:01:22,260 --> 00:01:24,930
- Can I help you? - Yes, are you the surgeon?
- Close enough, why?

20
00:01:24,980 --> 00:01:28,569
- Well, you know. - I don't know.
- There's a medical emergency.

21
00:01:28,620 --> 00:01:30,620
Will there be singing?

22
00:01:31,060 --> 00:01:33,289
- No.
- Fine, then.

23
00:01:33,340 --> 00:01:37,650
- We weren't sure where you'd come down.
- Sorry? - In your capsule.

24
00:01:37,700 --> 00:01:40,530
I'm never sure. I don't
like being sure about things.

25
00:01:40,579 --> 00:01:43,530
One minute you're sure, the
next everybody turns into lizards

26
00:01:43,579 --> 00:01:45,609
- and a piano falls on you.
- A piano?

27
00:01:45,659 --> 00:01:47,599
It's been a long day.

28
00:01:50,140 --> 00:01:51,849
Are you expecting a surgeon?

29
00:01:51,900 --> 00:01:53,849
So what's the medical emergency?

30
00:01:53,900 --> 00:01:56,049
Didn't you read the agreement?

31
00:01:56,099 --> 00:01:57,640
There it is.

32
00:01:59,420 --> 00:02:01,969
- What?
- There, that's it.

33
00:02:02,019 --> 00:02:03,659
That's what?

34
00:02:05,060 --> 00:02:07,170
Oh, the flying saucer.

35
00:02:07,219 --> 00:02:08,759
Is that new?

36
00:02:17,460 --> 00:02:19,050
Come on.

37
00:02:19,099 --> 00:02:21,569
Well, you took your time.

38
00:02:21,620 --> 00:02:24,009
Sorry, ma'am. This is him.

39
00:02:24,060 --> 00:02:25,610
- This is the surgeon.
- Hello.

40
00:02:25,659 --> 00:02:27,370
You don't look much like your pictures.

41
00:02:27,420 --> 00:02:28,930
That's an ongoing problem for me.

42
00:02:28,979 --> 00:02:30,770
Doesn't look very impressive, does he?

43
00:02:30,819 --> 00:02:32,770
Nardole, what HAVE you
brought to my doorstep?

44
00:02:32,819 --> 00:02:35,939
- I've had a haircut, this is my best suit.
- It's not even a suit.

45
00:02:37,460 --> 00:02:40,460
- Do I know you?
- You most certainly do not.

46
00:02:41,020 --> 00:02:44,409
And now that you've met me, you'll
do your very best to forget me.

47
00:02:44,460 --> 00:02:45,530
River!

48
00:02:45,579 --> 00:02:48,689
Oi! Dr Song to you.

49
00:02:48,740 --> 00:02:50,930
Sometimes Professor, but mainly Doctor.

50
00:02:50,979 --> 00:02:53,050
Don't use my name. Ever.

51
00:02:54,259 --> 00:02:57,370
- How do you know me?
- Well, it's a tiny bit complicated.

52
00:02:57,420 --> 00:03:00,370
- People usually need a flowchart.
- It doesn't matter.

53
00:03:00,419 --> 00:03:02,650
If either of you use my name again,

54
00:03:02,699 --> 00:03:06,050
I will remove your organs
in alphabetical order.

55
00:03:06,099 --> 00:03:08,610
- Any questions?
- Which alphabet?

56
00:03:08,659 --> 00:03:12,250
- Sorry, you really didn't want these questions, did you?
- This way.

57
00:03:12,300 --> 00:03:14,569
We don't have a lot of time.

58
00:03:15,020 --> 00:03:17,610
- What seems to be the problem?
- My husband.

59
00:03:17,659 --> 00:03:18,729
Your husband?

60
00:03:18,780 --> 00:03:22,050
Didn't you read my
message? My husband, yes.

61
00:03:22,099 --> 00:03:23,969
My husband is dying.

62
00:03:26,539 --> 00:03:28,280
Something wrong?

63
00:03:30,579 --> 00:03:33,579
I think I'm going to
need a bigger flowchart.

64
00:04:19,660 --> 00:04:21,769
Husband, I return to you.

65
00:04:21,819 --> 00:04:24,300
Where is my queen?

66
00:04:25,339 --> 00:04:27,209
Never far from you, my love.

67
00:04:27,259 --> 00:04:30,050
Aahhh.

68
00:04:30,100 --> 00:04:31,500
No, wait.

69
00:04:33,620 --> 00:04:36,250
- That's your husband?
- Listen, you are being watched

70
00:04:36,300 --> 00:04:37,569
by four billion people.

71
00:04:37,620 --> 00:04:40,689
You are surrounded by warrior
monks with sentient laser swords,

72
00:04:40,740 --> 00:04:43,449
genetically engineered anger
problems and not enough to do.

73
00:04:43,500 --> 00:04:46,209
Best just stay still and
keep your hands by your side.

74
00:04:46,259 --> 00:04:47,730
No, wait...

75
00:04:48,659 --> 00:04:51,370
- THAT's your husband?
- My husband, your patient.

76
00:04:51,420 --> 00:04:52,850
King Hydroflax.

77
00:04:52,899 --> 00:04:56,009
Yes, that's who you're
married to, not anybody else?

78
00:04:56,060 --> 00:04:58,850
My love, attend me, woman!

79
00:04:58,899 --> 00:05:00,689
I fly to you.

80
00:05:00,740 --> 00:05:02,009
Is there a problem?

81
00:05:02,060 --> 00:05:04,930
- Right, so you don't recognise me, then?
- Why would I recognise you?

82
00:05:04,980 --> 00:05:06,579
Oh, no reason.

83
00:05:08,740 --> 00:05:11,209
I don't like him. Do you like him?

84
00:05:11,259 --> 00:05:12,970
Don't cross your arms.

85
00:05:13,019 --> 00:05:14,490
He's a lying-down person.

86
00:05:14,540 --> 00:05:17,329
I don't like lying-down
people. It's so untidy.

87
00:05:17,379 --> 00:05:21,089
- Keep your arms by your side, like she said.
- My one true love!

88
00:05:21,139 --> 00:05:23,930
The only husband I will ever have.

89
00:05:23,980 --> 00:05:27,370
My time with you has been too short.

90
00:05:27,420 --> 00:05:30,209
You have given me days of adventure

91
00:05:30,259 --> 00:05:33,129
and many nights of passion.

92
00:05:33,180 --> 00:05:35,730
- Oh-oh!
- Why d'you keep crossing them?

93
00:05:35,779 --> 00:05:40,129
- Because they cross, I've got cross arms.
- The end is near. I feel it.

94
00:05:40,180 --> 00:05:43,850
Forgive me, my lord. I have
acted against your instructions.

95
00:05:43,899 --> 00:05:49,810
- My love?
- If you die this day, this galaxy will drown in tears.

96
00:05:49,860 --> 00:05:52,490
Look at them... your people!

97
00:05:52,540 --> 00:05:55,209
They watch and hope and pray.

98
00:05:55,259 --> 00:06:00,730
With so much at stake, I followed
my heart. I disobeyed your orders...

99
00:06:00,779 --> 00:06:07,129
and sent for the finest
surgeon in the galaxy!

100
00:06:24,100 --> 00:06:27,209
This might be an alarming
question in the circumstance,

101
00:06:27,259 --> 00:06:30,759
but... you really do think
I'm a surgeon, don't you?

102
00:06:31,500 --> 00:06:32,769
Oh...

103
00:06:32,819 --> 00:06:35,250
OK, calm down, keep it together.

104
00:06:35,300 --> 00:06:36,529
Don't make puddles.

105
00:06:36,579 --> 00:06:39,620
Surgeon. Attend your patient.

106
00:06:42,300 --> 00:06:43,740
Oh!

107
00:06:48,259 --> 00:06:50,569
Any tiny hint of species he might be?

108
00:06:50,620 --> 00:06:53,569
OK, never mind, you just stay there.

109
00:06:53,620 --> 00:06:56,220
You're probably going to need a mop.

110
00:06:58,740 --> 00:07:00,730
- Bow.
- Sorry, what?

111
00:07:00,779 --> 00:07:04,410
You are in the presence of his
Infinite Majesty, King Hydroflax.

112
00:07:04,459 --> 00:07:07,850
- You will bow.
- Oh, no, I'm sorry, Your Majesty, I can't do that.

113
00:07:07,899 --> 00:07:09,529
- You what?
- It's my back.

114
00:07:09,579 --> 00:07:11,889
- Your back?
- Yeah, my back's playing up.

115
00:07:11,939 --> 00:07:14,490
It simply refuses to carry the weight

116
00:07:14,540 --> 00:07:17,490
of an entirely pointless
stratum of society

117
00:07:17,540 --> 00:07:19,689
who contribute nothing
of worth to the world

118
00:07:19,740 --> 00:07:22,860
and crush the hopes and
dreams of working people.

119
00:07:27,339 --> 00:07:29,250
Can you save me, Surgeon?

120
00:07:29,300 --> 00:07:31,290
Well, that depends upon
what's wrong with you.

121
00:07:31,339 --> 00:07:33,970
- There's something in his brain.
- You could have fooled me.

122
00:07:34,019 --> 00:07:35,980
Oh, sorry.

123
00:07:38,379 --> 00:07:42,329
Sorry, just gallows humour.
Probably the wrong word.

124
00:07:42,379 --> 00:07:45,930
- Yeah, I would say it is.
- My love, you must rest.

125
00:07:45,980 --> 00:07:49,290
The surgeon and I will
discuss the procedure.

126
00:07:49,340 --> 00:07:54,529
Prepare, master of my life, to live anew.

127
00:07:56,659 --> 00:07:58,610
Patience be with you all.

128
00:07:58,659 --> 00:08:02,129
Our King will rise again!

129
00:08:02,180 --> 00:08:05,490
Our King will rise again.

130
00:08:05,540 --> 00:08:08,610
Our King will rise again!

131
00:08:08,660 --> 00:08:13,129
Hydroflax! Hydroflax!

132
00:08:13,180 --> 00:08:15,569
All right, enough of
this. The joke's over.

133
00:08:15,620 --> 00:08:17,089
- What joke?
- Look at me.

134
00:08:17,139 --> 00:08:18,339
Why?

135
00:08:19,379 --> 00:08:20,730
I'm the Doctor.

136
00:08:20,779 --> 00:08:24,279
You'd better be, you've got
an operation to perform.

137
00:08:24,500 --> 00:08:28,139
Here's the entry wound, just
below the hairline. And...

138
00:08:29,660 --> 00:08:31,009
there's the projectile.

139
00:08:31,060 --> 00:08:33,730
It should have killed him
straight off, but he's very strong.

140
00:08:33,779 --> 00:08:36,250
- That's not a bullet.
- It's a diamond.

141
00:08:36,299 --> 00:08:39,330
- How did it get in there?
- At speed.

142
00:08:39,379 --> 00:08:41,250
Do you recognise it?

143
00:08:42,179 --> 00:08:44,129
- No!
- Yes.

144
00:08:44,179 --> 00:08:46,409
- The Halassi Androvar.
- The very same.

145
00:08:46,460 --> 00:08:49,169
Hydroflax was leading the
raid on the Halassi vaults.

146
00:08:49,220 --> 00:08:52,129
In the ensuing firefight, the
whole thing blew up in his face,

147
00:08:52,179 --> 00:08:55,409
with the result that he now
has the most valuable diamond

148
00:08:55,460 --> 00:09:00,769
in the universe lodged three
inches inside his enormous head.

149
00:09:00,820 --> 00:09:02,100
So...

150
00:09:04,500 --> 00:09:05,929
can you remove it?

151
00:09:05,980 --> 00:09:09,049
It's very small, it might be
difficult to manoeuvre it.

152
00:09:09,100 --> 00:09:10,970
Not the diamond.

153
00:09:11,019 --> 00:09:12,539
His head!

154
00:09:14,460 --> 00:09:16,090
- His head?
- Yes.

155
00:09:16,139 --> 00:09:19,210
I think it would be easier just to
remove the whole thing, don't you?

156
00:09:19,259 --> 00:09:22,889
- Wouldn't that kill him?
- You're the medical expert, but I'd say so, yes.

157
00:09:22,940 --> 00:09:24,929
- Your husband?
- Sort of. - Sort of?

158
00:09:24,980 --> 00:09:26,769
I basically married the diamond.

159
00:09:26,820 --> 00:09:31,169
- The Halassi want their diamond back, so they came to me.
- Why?

160
00:09:31,220 --> 00:09:33,929
- I'm an archaeologist.
- Slash murderer slash thief.

161
00:09:33,980 --> 00:09:35,970
An archaeologist IS just a thief.

162
00:09:36,019 --> 00:09:39,129
With patience. Never had much of that.

163
00:09:39,179 --> 00:09:42,090
It'll fit in here, don't you
think? I've checked it for leaks.

164
00:09:42,139 --> 00:09:44,730
- Is this what you're like when I'm not...?
- Not what?

165
00:09:44,779 --> 00:09:47,049
You're talking about murdering someone.

166
00:09:47,100 --> 00:09:49,730
No, I'm not. I'm actually
murdering someone.

167
00:09:49,779 --> 00:09:52,940
Cheer up, get a saw, I'll kill
the lights, you kill the patient.

168
00:09:53,940 --> 00:09:56,330
I employed you! You agreed to this.

169
00:09:56,379 --> 00:10:00,330
Do you not know who that man is?

170
00:10:00,379 --> 00:10:03,250
King Hydroflax, the butcher
of the Bone Meadows,

171
00:10:03,299 --> 00:10:07,250
who ends his battles by eating
his enemies, dead or alive.

172
00:10:07,299 --> 00:10:08,809
The murder of a creature like that

173
00:10:08,860 --> 00:10:12,860
wouldn't weigh heavily on my
conscience, even if I had one.

174
00:10:12,940 --> 00:10:14,529
What's that face?

175
00:10:14,580 --> 00:10:17,529
Are you... thinking?

176
00:10:17,580 --> 00:10:21,330
- Stop it, you're a man, it looks weird.
- I need more information.

177
00:10:21,379 --> 00:10:23,370
- For what?
- For my diagnosis.

178
00:10:23,419 --> 00:10:25,769
He's dying. We're about to steal his head

179
00:10:25,820 --> 00:10:28,169
and scoop out his brains.
Aren't we overthinking?

180
00:10:28,220 --> 00:10:29,570
I'll be the judge of that.

181
00:10:29,620 --> 00:10:31,129
I'm the Doctor.

182
00:10:31,179 --> 00:10:33,850
You know who you remind me of?

183
00:10:33,899 --> 00:10:36,090
Yes, probably a chap with a big...

184
00:10:36,139 --> 00:10:38,100
My second wife.

185
00:10:50,500 --> 00:10:52,250
Darling!

186
00:10:52,299 --> 00:10:53,889
You're up and about!

187
00:10:53,940 --> 00:10:56,490
- False wife!
- How much better you're looking!

188
00:10:56,539 --> 00:10:57,850
You plan to take my head.

189
00:10:57,899 --> 00:10:59,929
Never crossed my mind. Is this your bag?

190
00:10:59,980 --> 00:11:02,860
Perhaps you should have just asked.

191
00:11:19,220 --> 00:11:23,490
Well! I wondered why we
didn't share a bathroom.

192
00:11:23,539 --> 00:11:26,090
You married a cyborg and
you didn't even know it.

193
00:11:26,139 --> 00:11:28,450
I'll have you flogged
and flayed and burnt.

194
00:11:28,500 --> 00:11:32,169
I will crush every last remnant
of you from this universe.

195
00:11:32,220 --> 00:11:34,210
How dare you! I'm your wife.

196
00:11:34,259 --> 00:11:36,809
- You planned to murder me!
- Don't change the subject.

197
00:11:36,860 --> 00:11:39,769
Why are you doing this? Who ARE you?

198
00:11:39,820 --> 00:11:41,409
I'm Professor River Song.

199
00:11:41,460 --> 00:11:44,529
You have an ancient artefact
of great value to good people,

200
00:11:44,580 --> 00:11:47,370
and whatever it takes, I'm
going to bring it home to them.

201
00:11:47,419 --> 00:11:51,409
You have stolen so much
from so many, King Hydroflax,

202
00:11:51,460 --> 00:11:54,169
and I'm the woman who's
going to steal it all back.

203
00:11:54,220 --> 00:11:55,850
What are you?!

204
00:11:55,899 --> 00:11:57,769
I'm an archaeologist.

205
00:11:57,820 --> 00:11:59,889
Look! I've got a trowel.

206
00:12:03,379 --> 00:12:06,049
- Ha-ha-ha!
- Do not harm her!

207
00:12:06,100 --> 00:12:09,210
If you know what's good for you,
do not lay a finger on that woman.

208
00:12:09,259 --> 00:12:11,129
Ignore him. Attack!

209
00:12:15,340 --> 00:12:19,129
- Garbage disposal, right? Get ready
to say, "Whee!" - Put me down.

210
00:12:19,179 --> 00:12:22,090
Back off from River
Song. Give the order now.

211
00:12:22,139 --> 00:12:24,250
Get yourself under control.

212
00:12:24,299 --> 00:12:26,440
Do not attack the female.

213
00:12:28,340 --> 00:12:30,490
Nobody move, or the head gets it!

214
00:12:30,539 --> 00:12:32,769
- Do you really have a shooty trowel?
- It's sonic.

215
00:12:32,820 --> 00:12:35,129
Sonic trowel, you realise
how ridiculous that sounds?

216
00:12:35,179 --> 00:12:37,929
- Their threats are empty! Destroy them!
- Negative.

217
00:12:37,980 --> 00:12:41,490
- 78 percent of significant tissue damage.
- Do as you're told!

218
00:12:41,539 --> 00:12:44,330
Decision overruled.
Recommendation... chill.

219
00:12:44,379 --> 00:12:46,409
Look at that, your body's
got a mind of its own.

220
00:12:46,460 --> 00:12:49,049
More like an on board computer
for the cybernetic component.

221
00:12:49,100 --> 00:12:51,730
Plus in-built flash drive and
vernacular friendly interface.

222
00:12:51,779 --> 00:12:53,409
- Cyber co-pilot.
- Mobile life support.

223
00:12:53,460 --> 00:12:55,129
- Sexy.
- It's not sexy.

224
00:12:55,179 --> 00:12:57,970
- Absolutely sexy.
- Why is everything sexy now?

225
00:12:58,019 --> 00:13:01,529
Speaking of which... Ramone, prep
for emergency extraction, two to go.

226
00:13:01,580 --> 00:13:04,730
- 'Standing by for teleport.'
- Put it in the bag. - Sorry?

227
00:13:04,779 --> 00:13:07,570
- The head. Put it in the bag.
- Do not put me in the bag.

228
00:13:07,620 --> 00:13:09,929
Quickly, do it. Ramone,
20 seconds to jump.

229
00:13:09,980 --> 00:13:11,730
I will not be placed into a bag!

230
00:13:11,779 --> 00:13:14,049
Stop shouting a minute
if you want to go face-up.

231
00:13:14,100 --> 00:13:16,529
You will be crushed!
You will be destroyed!

232
00:13:16,580 --> 00:13:19,450
- You will beg my infinite mercy!
- Oh, zip it!

233
00:13:19,500 --> 00:13:21,850
Try to follow me and I'll
put him in a blender.

234
00:13:21,899 --> 00:13:23,440
Ramone, now.

235
00:13:27,740 --> 00:13:30,610
They will be tracked. They will be found.

236
00:13:36,700 --> 00:13:38,460
Agh! Ohh!

237
00:13:39,700 --> 00:13:43,090
Ramone! Just once, can
you get the height right?

238
00:13:43,139 --> 00:13:44,529
'Sorry, Professor.'

239
00:13:44,580 --> 00:13:47,370
When I escape, I will bring
terror to you and your family.

240
00:13:47,419 --> 00:13:49,009
There is no escape from the...

241
00:13:49,059 --> 00:13:51,929
'I'm on it. The capsule is really close.'

242
00:13:52,139 --> 00:13:53,970
Is something funny?

243
00:13:54,019 --> 00:13:56,450
Who dares laugh at Hydroflax?

244
00:13:56,500 --> 00:13:59,250
You shall be crushed! You
shall scream in fear!

245
00:13:59,299 --> 00:14:02,730
- Let me out of this bag!
- This is a serious mission in a critical phase.

246
00:14:02,779 --> 00:14:04,690
There is nothing to laugh about here.

247
00:14:04,740 --> 00:14:09,049
We're being threatened by
a bag! By a head in a bag!

248
00:14:09,100 --> 00:14:13,059
I shall make dust of you. My
enemies are meat for the devouring!

249
00:14:15,700 --> 00:14:19,610
I can't approve of any of this, but
I haven't laughed in a long time.

250
00:14:19,659 --> 00:14:24,169
- Good for you.
- Prepare to die in agony and submit to my supremacy!

251
00:14:24,220 --> 00:14:26,500
Unzip this bag!

252
00:14:31,139 --> 00:14:33,210
- You know, don't you?
- Know what?

253
00:14:33,259 --> 00:14:35,860
Stop pretending. You know who I am.

254
00:14:36,980 --> 00:14:41,570
- Who are you?
- You know who I am, it's... it's... it's me. - Great.

255
00:14:41,620 --> 00:14:44,169
Who ARE you?

256
00:14:44,220 --> 00:14:45,940
Professor Song!

257
00:14:47,659 --> 00:14:49,809
Sorry, Professor, sorry
about the height thing.

258
00:14:49,860 --> 00:14:51,259
Prove it.

259
00:14:53,980 --> 00:14:56,779
Ugh!

260
00:14:59,299 --> 00:15:01,330
Doesn't it get dull after a while?

261
00:15:01,379 --> 00:15:04,649
As an activity, it's not
hugely varied, is it?

262
00:15:04,700 --> 00:15:06,769
I'm so sorry.

263
00:15:06,820 --> 00:15:09,649
This is my husband, Ramone.

264
00:15:09,700 --> 00:15:10,850
Another one?

265
00:15:10,899 --> 00:15:13,529
- Are you going to kill him, too?
- We're not actually married.

266
00:15:13,580 --> 00:15:16,610
- We are, in fact. I wiped it from your memory.
- Why?

267
00:15:16,659 --> 00:15:19,289
You were being annoying. So,
the Damsel, do we have a fix?

268
00:15:19,340 --> 00:15:22,929
Found the capsule just over in the
village, but I can't locate Damsel.

269
00:15:22,980 --> 00:15:25,649
- I've looked everywhere.
- Who's Damsel? - Have you been thorough?

270
00:15:25,700 --> 00:15:27,259
It's not easy... he does have 12 faces.

271
00:15:27,299 --> 00:15:30,809
None of these men are here. Are
you sure it's one of these?

272
00:15:30,860 --> 00:15:34,970
Yes! He only has these 12 faces.
He'll be around here somewhere.

273
00:15:35,019 --> 00:15:37,889
This is the closest intersection
with the Doctor's timeline.

274
00:15:37,940 --> 00:15:40,049
That's why I crashed
Hydroflax's ship here.

275
00:15:40,100 --> 00:15:43,330
- Damsel.
- Codename... "Damsel in Distress".

276
00:15:43,379 --> 00:15:45,529
Apparently, he needs a lot of rescuing.

277
00:15:45,580 --> 00:15:49,169
What if he has a face that
you don't know about yet?

278
00:15:49,220 --> 00:15:50,769
He has limits.

279
00:15:50,820 --> 00:15:53,419
Well, then, let's go find him.

280
00:15:55,940 --> 00:15:59,889
- You are in league with the former Queen.
- She employed me!

281
00:15:59,940 --> 00:16:02,970
- I didn't really know anything.
- You have information.

282
00:16:03,019 --> 00:16:05,769
Oh, hardly anything, really. A tiny bit.

283
00:16:05,820 --> 00:16:08,049
You will give this information to us.

284
00:16:08,100 --> 00:16:11,610
- Oh, absolutely! Course I will.
- We will take the information.

285
00:16:11,659 --> 00:16:12,929
Anything you like.

286
00:16:12,980 --> 00:16:16,330
- I'll even write it down for you.
- That will not be necessary.

287
00:16:16,379 --> 00:16:19,970
You will be uploaded. We
apologise for the inconvenience.

288
00:16:20,019 --> 00:16:22,210
Uploaded? How?

289
00:16:22,259 --> 00:16:24,179
Recommendation...

290
00:16:25,379 --> 00:16:26,769
hold still.

291
00:16:26,820 --> 00:16:28,700
Ooh-ooh!

292
00:16:31,820 --> 00:16:35,289
No, this is no good. I don't like this.

293
00:16:35,340 --> 00:16:38,809
- Your cooperation is appreciated.
- I never agreed!

294
00:16:38,860 --> 00:16:41,330
No, this is unfair.

295
00:16:41,379 --> 00:16:42,929
Pursuit now commences.

296
00:16:42,980 --> 00:16:45,009
This is too tall!

297
00:16:45,059 --> 00:16:46,929
I'm afraid of heights.

298
00:16:46,980 --> 00:16:49,779
Recommendation... close your eyes.

299
00:16:54,220 --> 00:16:56,500
Aaargh!

300
00:16:58,860 --> 00:17:02,169
What if we can't find him? We
need to get you off-world now.

301
00:17:02,220 --> 00:17:05,369
"Off-world"? People never
say that. Are you new?

302
00:17:05,420 --> 00:17:07,369
We can't hang around
waiting, he could be ages.

303
00:17:07,420 --> 00:17:09,529
Yes, he's probably off
rebuilding a civilisation

304
00:17:09,579 --> 00:17:11,450
or defeating giant robot fish...

305
00:17:11,500 --> 00:17:14,690
- We'll just have to steal it.
- .. from the ninth dimension. Sorry, what?

306
00:17:14,740 --> 00:17:15,930
The hopper is really close,

307
00:17:15,980 --> 00:17:18,609
- we'd be out of here in less than ten minutes.
- I need time travel.

308
00:17:18,660 --> 00:17:21,130
- I need this TARDIS!
- I'm sorry, the word "steal",

309
00:17:21,180 --> 00:17:22,690
- somebody said "steal".
- Yes.

310
00:17:22,740 --> 00:17:27,049
We're going to steal this box.
Hush, you wouldn't understand.

311
00:17:27,099 --> 00:17:28,849
You can't.

312
00:17:28,900 --> 00:17:32,089
- Why can't I?
- You can't just steal a TA... a box. - Why not?

313
00:17:32,140 --> 00:17:35,569
- Look, it says "Police".
- I have a key.

314
00:17:35,619 --> 00:17:40,250
OK, this Damsel person, he sounds...
he sounds pretty dangerous...

315
00:17:40,299 --> 00:17:41,569
ish.

316
00:17:41,619 --> 00:17:44,130
It's a... time... machine.

317
00:17:44,180 --> 00:17:46,529
I can take it, do whatever I
want for as long as I like

318
00:17:46,579 --> 00:17:49,369
and pop it back a second later,
he'll never know it was gone.

319
00:17:49,420 --> 00:17:51,490
- Yes, he will.
- How?

320
00:17:51,539 --> 00:17:55,140
- He'll just know.
- Well, he's never noticed before.

321
00:17:55,779 --> 00:17:58,619
Maybe... he'll notice now.

322
00:18:01,940 --> 00:18:04,279
I'll see you on Temple Beach.

323
00:18:05,740 --> 00:18:07,970
I've already picked out your swimwear.

324
00:18:08,019 --> 00:18:11,769
- OK, but be careful.
- Absolutely not.

325
00:18:11,819 --> 00:18:14,299
You, with me. Bring the head.

326
00:18:15,299 --> 00:18:17,819
Please, look after her for me.

327
00:18:22,259 --> 00:18:25,930
Oh, before you come in, you'd
better prepare yourself for a shock.

328
00:18:25,980 --> 00:18:28,900
It's not as... snug as it looks.

329
00:18:35,460 --> 00:18:37,009
Finally.

330
00:18:37,059 --> 00:18:39,369
Finally?

331
00:18:39,420 --> 00:18:41,059
It's my go.

332
00:18:43,700 --> 00:18:49,210
Oh... my... God!

333
00:18:49,259 --> 00:18:50,569
It's bigger!

334
00:18:50,619 --> 00:18:52,170
- Well, yes.
- On the inside!

335
00:18:52,220 --> 00:18:53,930
- We need to concentrate.
- Than it is!

336
00:18:53,980 --> 00:18:56,690
I know where you're going with
this, but I need you to calm down.

337
00:18:56,740 --> 00:18:59,490
- On the outside!
- You've certainly grasped the essentials.

338
00:18:59,539 --> 00:19:03,890
My entire understanding of physical
space has been transformed!

339
00:19:03,940 --> 00:19:07,329
Three-dimensional Euclidean
geometry has been torn up,

340
00:19:07,380 --> 00:19:10,250
thrown in the air and snogged to death!

341
00:19:10,299 --> 00:19:15,609
My grasp of the universal
constants of physical reality

342
00:19:15,660 --> 00:19:17,579
has been changed...

343
00:19:19,339 --> 00:19:20,809
forever.

344
00:19:22,299 --> 00:19:23,369
Sorry.

345
00:19:23,420 --> 00:19:25,690
I've always wanted to
see that done properly.

346
00:19:25,740 --> 00:19:28,490
Would you like a drink? Aldebaran brandy.

347
00:19:28,539 --> 00:19:30,369
Help yourself, but don't tell Dad.

348
00:19:30,420 --> 00:19:32,339
What's that noise?

349
00:19:34,380 --> 00:19:37,130
It seems to have powered
down, conserving batteries.

350
00:19:37,180 --> 00:19:38,809
It's an in-built life-support system.

351
00:19:38,859 --> 00:19:41,220
- I'm not sure what powers it, but...
- I really don't care.

352
00:19:41,259 --> 00:19:43,930
- What's that noise?
- I don't know. A signal? Distress call?

353
00:19:43,980 --> 00:19:46,890
- Homing beacon. - Possibly.
- So the rest of him is coming?

354
00:19:46,940 --> 00:19:50,849
- He must be very cross... he's lost his head.
- Time we were off then.

355
00:19:56,299 --> 00:19:59,400
- You're doing it wrong.
- I am certainly not.

356
00:20:01,299 --> 00:20:03,009
Not those levers.

357
00:20:03,059 --> 00:20:04,259
Hush.

358
00:20:06,180 --> 00:20:08,930
- You probably want to press that button.
- Why?!

359
00:20:08,980 --> 00:20:11,329
That evacuates the waste
tank on deck seven.

360
00:20:11,380 --> 00:20:13,130
- Does it?
- What is wrong with you?

361
00:20:13,180 --> 00:20:14,930
Better avoid deck seven then.

362
00:20:14,980 --> 00:20:17,130
Something's interfering with the engines,

363
00:20:17,180 --> 00:20:18,970
which is technically not possible.

364
00:20:19,019 --> 00:20:20,769
- Maybe.
- How would you know?

365
00:20:20,819 --> 00:20:23,329
Maybe the engines are
interfering with themselves.

366
00:20:23,380 --> 00:20:26,569
Wild theory, but what if this
machine had certain safeguards.

367
00:20:26,619 --> 00:20:30,210
For instance, maybe it can't take
off when a life form registers

368
00:20:30,259 --> 00:20:33,049
as being both inside and
outside at the same time?

369
00:20:33,099 --> 00:20:34,569
Head and body.

370
00:20:34,619 --> 00:20:40,170
Which would mean... and again,
I'm just wildly theorising here...

371
00:20:40,220 --> 00:20:43,329
that's the door would not engage properly.

372
00:20:43,380 --> 00:20:46,849
Of course. It can't seal
the real-time envelope.

373
00:20:46,900 --> 00:20:49,529
Hence it can't take off.

374
00:20:49,579 --> 00:20:53,130
Not when someone is in
and out at the same time.

375
00:20:53,180 --> 00:20:57,369
- I mean, that just wouldn't be good manners, would it?
- You're very quick.

376
00:20:57,420 --> 00:20:59,009
Yes.

377
00:20:59,059 --> 00:21:00,650
For a Doctor.

378
00:21:00,700 --> 00:21:02,220
Yes.

379
00:21:03,579 --> 00:21:05,059
Seriously?

380
00:21:09,660 --> 00:21:10,930
Hello?

381
00:21:10,980 --> 00:21:13,299
Hello, is that you?

382
00:21:14,700 --> 00:21:17,500
- Nardole, is that you?
- It's me, yes.

383
00:21:18,220 --> 00:21:22,420
- Please, you've got to help me.
- What's wrong? Where are you?

384
00:21:23,819 --> 00:21:27,529
In the alleyway. Can't you
see me? Come a bit closer.

385
00:21:27,579 --> 00:21:30,319
- What are you doing there?
- Help me.

386
00:21:31,500 --> 00:21:32,730
Are you injured?

387
00:21:32,779 --> 00:21:35,220
Well, er... yes.

388
00:21:38,539 --> 00:21:42,170
Sorry. So sorry. It made me!

389
00:21:42,220 --> 00:21:46,809
- Nardole, why are you pointing a gun at your own head?
- It's not my head!

390
00:21:46,859 --> 00:21:51,140
- Well, it is my head, but it's not my gun.
- What happened to you? - Please.

391
00:21:52,180 --> 00:21:54,009
Just do as it says.

392
00:21:54,059 --> 00:21:55,890
It's signalling.

393
00:21:55,940 --> 00:21:59,329
- We have to assume the body is homing in on this.
- So, how do we stop it?

394
00:21:59,380 --> 00:22:01,089
Well, we could chop his head off.

395
00:22:01,140 --> 00:22:02,849
- Oh, look...
- Does sarcasm help?

396
00:22:02,900 --> 00:22:05,450
- Wouldn't it be a great universe if it did?
- So, summing up,

397
00:22:05,500 --> 00:22:06,890
it's coming, we can't take off,

398
00:22:06,940 --> 00:22:08,890
- we can't seal the doors.
- Yep.

399
00:22:08,940 --> 00:22:12,009
So... we just kill the head, right?

400
00:22:12,059 --> 00:22:14,130
- You can't shoot the head in the face!
- Why not?

401
00:22:14,180 --> 00:22:16,380
Aaarrgh!

402
00:22:17,460 --> 00:22:19,569
Go on, then, tell him to put his hands up.

403
00:22:19,619 --> 00:22:23,009
- Do not fire if you value your lives.
- Why, what are you going to do?

404
00:22:23,059 --> 00:22:25,970
Kill me, and my body will burn.

405
00:22:26,019 --> 00:22:29,130
- Burn what?
- This world!

406
00:22:29,180 --> 00:22:32,970
Inquiry... are you acquainted
with the criminal River Song?

407
00:22:33,019 --> 00:22:34,529
That wasn't me, that was him!

408
00:22:34,579 --> 00:22:37,930
Repeat, are you acquainted
with the criminal River Song?

409
00:22:37,980 --> 00:22:40,009
Please, just answer it.

410
00:22:40,059 --> 00:22:41,569
Yes.

411
00:22:41,619 --> 00:22:44,220
You will take River Song a message.

412
00:22:45,259 --> 00:22:46,690
What message?

413
00:22:46,740 --> 00:22:48,569
Suppose we believe you... how?

414
00:22:48,619 --> 00:22:51,130
My body contains a split
quantum actualiser.

415
00:22:51,180 --> 00:22:53,930
A perpetually stabilised black
hole... that's your power source.

416
00:22:53,980 --> 00:22:55,809
What sort of medical school did you go to?

417
00:22:55,859 --> 00:22:58,250
- A really good one for doctors.
- More than a power source.

418
00:22:58,299 --> 00:23:01,089
- If necessary, a bomb.
- So you could wipe out this solar system.

419
00:23:01,140 --> 00:23:03,450
- It wouldn't be the first.
- It would be your last.

420
00:23:03,500 --> 00:23:07,130
- A fitting end for the glory of Hydroflax.
- So, why haven't you threatened this before?

421
00:23:07,180 --> 00:23:09,730
A king does not endanger
his people for no reason.

422
00:23:09,779 --> 00:23:11,890
- You're endangering them now.
- I'm cross.

423
00:23:11,940 --> 00:23:14,289
Dr Song, are you there?

424
00:23:14,339 --> 00:23:17,700
- I have a message for you.
- Ramone! Get in here!

425
00:23:19,660 --> 00:23:22,339
- Ahh!
- You're going to die!

426
00:23:28,619 --> 00:23:31,289
- Kill her. - No!
- Put her down.

427
00:23:31,339 --> 00:23:32,529
Kill her now!

428
00:23:32,579 --> 00:23:33,930
Death initiating.

429
00:23:33,980 --> 00:23:35,579
I'm so sorry!

430
00:23:40,740 --> 00:23:42,529
I'm sorry!

431
00:23:42,579 --> 00:23:45,059
Stop them! Stop them!

432
00:23:46,619 --> 00:23:49,130
- Where are we going?
- Get the hell out!

433
00:23:49,180 --> 00:23:51,410
- Stop them!
- Death initiating.

434
00:23:51,460 --> 00:23:55,220
- You set the coordinates... where for?
- Just get the damn head!

435
00:23:56,339 --> 00:23:59,460
Kill them! Destroy them!

436
00:24:02,220 --> 00:24:04,420
- Kill them!
- Here.

437
00:24:06,099 --> 00:24:07,460
With me.

438
00:24:08,660 --> 00:24:11,650
- Where are we? - This way, come on.
- What about the box?

439
00:24:11,700 --> 00:24:14,329
Stop holding my hand,
people don't do that to me.

440
00:24:14,380 --> 00:24:15,890
- Hush.
- Don't hush me.

441
00:24:15,940 --> 00:24:18,220
I'm not a hushing person.

442
00:24:29,619 --> 00:24:33,660
'We are currently cruising
at warp factor 12.'

443
00:24:35,740 --> 00:24:39,259
'Traversing the fourth galaxy
of our seven-galaxy cruise.'

444
00:24:40,460 --> 00:24:43,019
'Next is the Andromeda galaxy.'

445
00:24:49,700 --> 00:24:53,460
'Supernova approaching now to starboard.'

446
00:24:56,700 --> 00:24:58,410
Ah, Dr Song.

447
00:24:58,460 --> 00:25:00,329
Your table is ready.

448
00:25:00,380 --> 00:25:03,450
Flemming! How are the twins?

449
00:25:03,500 --> 00:25:05,890
Still digesting their mother,
thank you for asking.

450
00:25:05,940 --> 00:25:08,930
- I'm sure it was a lovely ceremony.
- Oh, there were tears.

451
00:25:08,980 --> 00:25:11,319
And just a hint of screaming.

452
00:25:12,700 --> 00:25:15,369
Er, Flemming, I wonder,

453
00:25:15,420 --> 00:25:18,450
could you deadlock seal
the baggage hold for me?

454
00:25:18,500 --> 00:25:22,049
It's a little irregular. The other
passengers might want access.

455
00:25:22,099 --> 00:25:25,569
Do you remember that time I
was transporting dragon eggs?

456
00:25:25,619 --> 00:25:27,359
Consider it done.

457
00:25:29,660 --> 00:25:32,089
Is the gentleman here for dinner?

458
00:25:32,140 --> 00:25:33,849
- Yes, he is.
- Excellent!

459
00:25:33,900 --> 00:25:36,690
- I'll have the chef prepare him immediately.
- No, you won't.

460
00:25:36,740 --> 00:25:39,130
He will in fact be joining me to eat.

461
00:25:39,180 --> 00:25:43,490
I was about to suggest that
force-feeding might be required.

462
00:25:43,539 --> 00:25:46,170
This way. Oh, may I take your bag?

463
00:25:46,220 --> 00:25:48,490
Oh, no, that's fine, Thanks.

464
00:25:51,819 --> 00:25:54,099
Sorry. It was my stomach.

465
00:25:56,299 --> 00:25:59,009
I have an irritable bowel.

466
00:25:59,059 --> 00:26:00,650
My revenge will be merciless!

467
00:26:00,700 --> 00:26:03,569
- I will rip you open and devour you!
- It's having a day.

468
00:26:03,619 --> 00:26:05,859
You cannot escape!

469
00:26:07,619 --> 00:26:10,650
- This way.
- Your actions will not go unpunished!

470
00:26:10,700 --> 00:26:12,130
Here.

471
00:26:12,180 --> 00:26:15,539
- Ow!
- I don't suppose you mind if I freshen up.

472
00:26:17,900 --> 00:26:21,130
- Not bad for 200, eh?
- 200?

473
00:26:21,180 --> 00:26:24,089
I have an augmented lifespan. Long story.

474
00:26:24,140 --> 00:26:28,130
- So, what's the occasion?
- I've got the diamond, now it's time to sell it.

475
00:26:28,180 --> 00:26:30,289
I thought you were returning
it to the Halassi?

476
00:26:30,339 --> 00:26:33,210
Tell me, were you born boring,
or did you have to work at it?

477
00:26:33,259 --> 00:26:34,730
Where did you find a buyer?

478
00:26:34,779 --> 00:26:36,849
Look around you.

479
00:26:36,900 --> 00:26:38,809
The starship Harmony And Redemption,

480
00:26:38,859 --> 00:26:40,849
minimum ticket price one billion credits,

481
00:26:40,900 --> 00:26:43,890
plus the provable murder of
multiple innocent life forms.

482
00:26:43,940 --> 00:26:46,490
Suites are reserved for planet-burners.

483
00:26:46,539 --> 00:26:47,849
Thank you.

484
00:26:47,900 --> 00:26:51,049
Even the staff are required
to have a verifiable history

485
00:26:51,099 --> 00:26:52,849
of indiscriminate slaughter.

486
00:26:52,900 --> 00:26:56,529
This is where genocide comes
to kick back and relax.

487
00:26:56,579 --> 00:26:58,339
Do try the fish.

488
00:27:06,299 --> 00:27:08,640
Mr Flemming, there's an issue.

489
00:27:19,619 --> 00:27:21,559
Why are you frowning?

490
00:27:22,779 --> 00:27:24,130
How did you know?

491
00:27:24,180 --> 00:27:25,450
It's audible.

492
00:27:25,500 --> 00:27:28,170
Deadlock seals can be broken.

493
00:27:28,220 --> 00:27:29,730
By geniuses.

494
00:27:29,779 --> 00:27:32,289
Hydroflax has a brain the size of a pea

495
00:27:32,339 --> 00:27:34,289
and it's currently under the table.

496
00:27:34,339 --> 00:27:36,369
He's gone back to sleep, I think.

497
00:27:36,420 --> 00:27:39,130
- You married him, though.
- I told you, I married the diamond.

498
00:27:39,180 --> 00:27:41,289
- How?
- I posed as his nurse.

499
00:27:41,339 --> 00:27:43,329
- Took me a week.
- To fall in love?

500
00:27:43,380 --> 00:27:46,369
It's the easiest lie you can tell a man.

501
00:27:46,420 --> 00:27:50,380
They'll automatically believe
any story they're the hero of.

502
00:27:55,539 --> 00:27:57,690
River, there's, er...

503
00:27:57,740 --> 00:28:00,170
there's something I
should probably tell you.

504
00:28:00,220 --> 00:28:03,289
Dr Song, your guest has docked,

505
00:28:03,339 --> 00:28:05,289
he should be with you
in a very few minutes.

506
00:28:05,339 --> 00:28:07,930
- Thank you. Whenever he's ready.
- Of course.

507
00:28:07,980 --> 00:28:09,720
What's the book?

508
00:28:10,500 --> 00:28:12,809
Oh, it's my diary.

509
00:28:12,859 --> 00:28:16,609
One should always have something
sensational to read on a spaceship.

510
00:28:16,660 --> 00:28:18,130
Is it sad?

511
00:28:20,779 --> 00:28:23,930
- Why would a diary be sad?
- I don't know, it's just that...

512
00:28:23,980 --> 00:28:25,900
you look sad.

513
00:28:30,220 --> 00:28:31,650
It's nearly full.

514
00:28:31,700 --> 00:28:33,059
So?

515
00:28:36,259 --> 00:28:39,569
The man who gave me this was
the sort of man who'd know

516
00:28:39,619 --> 00:28:43,460
exactly how long a diary
you were going to need.

517
00:28:49,380 --> 00:28:50,890
He sounds awful.

518
00:28:50,940 --> 00:28:54,289
I suppose he is. I've never
really thought about it.

519
00:28:54,339 --> 00:28:56,619
Not somebody special then?

520
00:28:59,099 --> 00:29:00,539
No.

521
00:29:02,220 --> 00:29:04,960
But terribly useful every now and then.

522
00:29:09,460 --> 00:29:11,930
Please! I just need you
to get me out of here.

523
00:29:11,980 --> 00:29:14,609
He's in the main hold, sir,
but you've deadlocked it.

524
00:29:14,660 --> 00:29:18,009
If you don't mind be observing,
sir, you do seem a little nervous.

525
00:29:18,059 --> 00:29:20,089
Is someone threatening you?

526
00:29:20,140 --> 00:29:21,809
I'm the only one here.

527
00:29:21,859 --> 00:29:25,769
- Confirmed, sir, there's only one reading in the hold.
- I'm on my way.

528
00:29:25,819 --> 00:29:29,980
- Be careful, sir.
- Don't worry, I'll just stick my head round the door.

529
00:29:31,859 --> 00:29:36,420
- So who is this buyer?
- No idea, he just responded to the advert.

530
00:29:42,059 --> 00:29:44,809
- Which of you is Song?
- Who wants to know?

531
00:29:44,859 --> 00:29:46,410
I am Scratch.

532
00:29:46,460 --> 00:29:48,890
Don't need your name. Are
you empowered to purchase?

533
00:29:48,940 --> 00:29:51,329
I represent the Shoal
of the Winter Harmony.

534
00:29:51,380 --> 00:29:54,049
Don't care, don't want to know.
I'll need immediate payment.

535
00:29:54,099 --> 00:29:55,970
- Can you do that?
- And could you either sit down

536
00:29:56,019 --> 00:29:58,759
or fetch us the wine list or something?

537
00:30:03,380 --> 00:30:06,329
- You have the diamond?
- Of course I have the diamond.

538
00:30:06,380 --> 00:30:08,180
Show me the money.

539
00:30:24,259 --> 00:30:27,819
Just a thought, you probably
shouldn't do that in a restaurant.

540
00:30:42,940 --> 00:30:46,609
Once instructed, this will
transfer the necessary funds

541
00:30:46,660 --> 00:30:48,930
- to whatever account you choose.
- Thank you.

542
00:30:48,980 --> 00:30:50,769
The diamond.

543
00:30:50,819 --> 00:30:52,849
You're going to have to dig for it a bit,

544
00:30:52,900 --> 00:30:56,009
but somehow I don't think that's
going to be a problem for you.

545
00:30:56,059 --> 00:30:58,970
- Is this a deception?
- No. The diamond is in there.

546
00:30:59,019 --> 00:31:01,690
This is a public place,
there won't be any tricks.

547
00:31:01,740 --> 00:31:03,980
This is not a public place.

548
00:31:12,059 --> 00:31:15,170
- Block booking, that's clever.
- You needn't have bothered.

549
00:31:15,220 --> 00:31:16,490
I've brought what you want.

550
00:31:16,539 --> 00:31:18,970
Please do assume that I
have also taken precautions,

551
00:31:19,019 --> 00:31:21,569
and don't do anything that might
make me cross and kill you.

552
00:31:21,619 --> 00:31:23,210
Statement accepted.

553
00:31:23,259 --> 00:31:25,569
The diamond is here?

554
00:31:28,140 --> 00:31:29,940
The payment, then.

555
00:31:31,019 --> 00:31:35,089
100 billion credits. As we agreed.

556
00:31:35,140 --> 00:31:38,569
- This accesses all the banks in the galaxy.
- Thank you.

557
00:31:38,619 --> 00:31:40,210
Here you go, then.

558
00:31:40,259 --> 00:31:44,690
You may need to use a spoon or
knitting needle or something.

559
00:31:44,740 --> 00:31:48,609
- Be it known, we do not do this for ourselves.
- I really don't care.

560
00:31:48,660 --> 00:31:52,009
We do it in honour of our
distant and loving King,

561
00:31:52,059 --> 00:31:55,490
who once visited our
world in blood and joy.

562
00:31:55,539 --> 00:31:57,009
Well, isn't that lovely?

563
00:31:57,059 --> 00:32:00,890
We honour thee, we prostrate
ourselves in your name...

564
00:32:00,940 --> 00:32:02,410
Hydroflax.

565
00:32:02,460 --> 00:32:03,730
Hydroflax!

566
00:32:03,779 --> 00:32:08,289
For love of thee, we do
this thing today. Hydroflax.

567
00:32:08,339 --> 00:32:10,730
Hydroflax!

568
00:32:10,779 --> 00:32:13,170
Hydroflax! Hydroflax!

569
00:32:13,220 --> 00:32:15,529
Hydroflax!

570
00:32:15,579 --> 00:32:18,609
Give it. Give us the treasure.

571
00:32:18,660 --> 00:32:22,289
Hydroflax! Hydroflax! Hydroflax!

572
00:32:22,339 --> 00:32:24,369
What is wrong?

573
00:32:24,420 --> 00:32:26,569
Er... well, er...

574
00:32:26,619 --> 00:32:27,980
awkward.

575
00:32:30,740 --> 00:32:34,089
- I beg of you, not my head!
- Information is required.

576
00:32:34,140 --> 00:32:37,009
You know of River Song, wife of Hydroflax?

577
00:32:37,980 --> 00:32:40,970
I do. I know River Song of old.

578
00:32:41,019 --> 00:32:46,049
And if you spare me, I'll tell
you who she's really married to.

579
00:32:46,099 --> 00:32:48,289
- Explain.
- You need a head.

580
00:32:48,339 --> 00:32:51,849
I can get you a head... fit for a king.

581
00:32:51,900 --> 00:32:55,500
Why do you delay? We have
paid, we will receive.

582
00:32:56,819 --> 00:32:58,210
Yes, you will.

583
00:32:58,259 --> 00:33:00,809
Of... by jingo, you will, yes, of course.

584
00:33:00,859 --> 00:33:05,809
- But obviously, we have to, you know, er, check some...
- Things.

585
00:33:05,859 --> 00:33:09,170
Things. There are things that have
to be checked before I get it to you.

586
00:33:09,220 --> 00:33:11,130
If we don't check the thing, then...

587
00:33:11,180 --> 00:33:12,849
We will receive!

588
00:33:12,900 --> 00:33:15,890
Yes, you will receive, and here it is.

589
00:33:15,940 --> 00:33:18,690
Now, on its way.

590
00:33:18,740 --> 00:33:21,650
- This small distance.
- We will receive!

591
00:33:21,700 --> 00:33:22,970
Here you go.

592
00:33:23,019 --> 00:33:25,210
And you can have the bag as well.

593
00:33:25,259 --> 00:33:28,329
You know, it's been... lovely.

594
00:33:28,380 --> 00:33:32,210
But we don't want to intrude
on this special moment,

595
00:33:32,259 --> 00:33:35,529
so why don't we just leave
you with the new baby...?

596
00:33:35,579 --> 00:33:37,730
You will remain.

597
00:33:37,779 --> 00:33:40,009
Is that strictly necessary?

598
00:33:40,059 --> 00:33:42,900
I do not like... surprises.

599
00:33:45,980 --> 00:33:48,720
Well, it's going to be a funny old day.

600
00:33:50,019 --> 00:33:51,359
Oh, boy.

601
00:33:52,460 --> 00:33:55,890
You know what? I just can't stand
idly by and let this continue.

602
00:33:55,940 --> 00:33:58,299
Death has been done this day!

603
00:33:59,339 --> 00:34:02,890
Noble blood has been spilled.

604
00:34:02,940 --> 00:34:05,849
And our tears will surely follow.

605
00:34:05,900 --> 00:34:08,690
The sky shall crack,

606
00:34:08,739 --> 00:34:11,289
the ground shall heave,

607
00:34:11,340 --> 00:34:15,849
and even the rocks and the stones

608
00:34:15,900 --> 00:34:18,650
shall weep their rage.

609
00:34:18,699 --> 00:34:20,369
Behold!

610
00:34:20,420 --> 00:34:23,860
The head of Hydroflax!

611
00:34:27,500 --> 00:34:30,530
Rest now, sweet prince.

612
00:34:30,579 --> 00:34:34,460
Walk amongst us nevermore.

613
00:34:36,099 --> 00:34:38,889
Shall we start the bidding at 200 billion?

614
00:34:38,940 --> 00:34:40,409
I'm sorry, Professor Song,

615
00:34:40,460 --> 00:34:43,650
but we really couldn't keep this
treasure from the truly devout.

616
00:34:43,699 --> 00:34:46,050
My apologies to the truly devout.

617
00:34:46,099 --> 00:34:49,530
- Shall we find out who is the most truly devout?
- This is heresy!

618
00:34:49,579 --> 00:34:52,690
- 200 over there.
- 250 million by the sweet trolley.

619
00:34:52,739 --> 00:34:54,570
Silence! This is not our way.

620
00:34:54,619 --> 00:34:57,929
It doesn't say much for your king if
you can't put a price on his head.

621
00:34:57,980 --> 00:35:00,289
Let us see what the
king himself has to say.

622
00:35:00,340 --> 00:35:03,460
Aaargh!

623
00:35:05,300 --> 00:35:06,619
Quick!

624
00:35:07,820 --> 00:35:10,920
Professor Song! Has the
food disappointed you?

625
00:35:17,900 --> 00:35:20,699
At last, I am whole again.

626
00:35:22,699 --> 00:35:25,900
Come to me, my body.

627
00:35:33,739 --> 00:35:35,369
Well? Put me back.

628
00:35:35,420 --> 00:35:37,489
Scan in progress.

629
00:35:37,539 --> 00:35:40,250
You don't need to scan
me, just put me back.

630
00:35:40,300 --> 00:35:43,170
Tissue deterioration now irreversible.

631
00:35:43,219 --> 00:35:45,369
What are you going to do about that?

632
00:35:45,420 --> 00:35:48,610
Additional, the projectile inside
your brain continues to move.

633
00:35:48,659 --> 00:35:51,210
Prognosis... death in seven minutes.

634
00:35:51,260 --> 00:35:52,730
Well, I refuse.

635
00:35:52,780 --> 00:35:55,489
King Hydroflax does not accept death.

636
00:35:55,539 --> 00:35:57,130
Orders requested.

637
00:35:57,179 --> 00:36:00,130
Whatever I need to survive, do it. Now.

638
00:36:00,179 --> 00:36:03,849
- Orders accepted. You need a new head.
- No!

639
00:36:03,900 --> 00:36:06,650
No. Not a new head!

640
00:36:06,699 --> 00:36:08,250
Orders implementing.

641
00:36:08,300 --> 00:36:10,739
No. No...!

642
00:36:17,860 --> 00:36:21,380
I don't suppose you could fetch
that over for me, could you?

643
00:36:24,699 --> 00:36:27,090
As I was saying, Your Majesty.

644
00:36:27,139 --> 00:36:29,739
Well, your remaining Majesty.

645
00:36:32,579 --> 00:36:36,730
If it's a new head you're after,
this is the guide to the very best.

646
00:36:36,780 --> 00:36:40,250
- Don't touch that. Give that back to me.
- The diary of River Song.

647
00:36:40,300 --> 00:36:43,929
The ultimate guide to the
Time Lord known as the Doctor.

648
00:36:43,980 --> 00:36:46,119
Don't you dare touch that!

649
00:36:47,019 --> 00:36:49,820
Long live the King.

650
00:36:51,179 --> 00:36:53,210
"The Pandorica Opens."

651
00:36:53,260 --> 00:36:55,400
Ooh, that sounds exciting.

652
00:36:56,059 --> 00:36:58,530
And goodness me, a picnic at Asgard.

653
00:36:58,579 --> 00:37:01,409
Some people really know
how to snack, don't they?

654
00:37:01,460 --> 00:37:04,210
You should know, I have a
significant history of escaping.

655
00:37:04,260 --> 00:37:07,849
"The Crash of the Byzantium."
Didn't they make a movie of that?

656
00:37:07,900 --> 00:37:10,690
And when I do, I'm going to kill you.

657
00:37:10,739 --> 00:37:14,530
Oh, Jim the Fish! Well,
we all know Jim the Fish.

658
00:37:14,579 --> 00:37:17,130
And the longer you spend reading my diary,

659
00:37:17,179 --> 00:37:18,530
the longer I'm going to take.

660
00:37:18,579 --> 00:37:21,780
And you've just been to Manhattan.

661
00:37:22,780 --> 00:37:24,210
What planet is that?

662
00:37:24,260 --> 00:37:26,460
So do, please, keep going.

663
00:37:27,500 --> 00:37:28,929
This is irrelevant.

664
00:37:28,980 --> 00:37:31,090
If I may intrude, Your Majesty.

665
00:37:31,139 --> 00:37:34,690
The Doctor is a legendary
being of remarkable power

666
00:37:34,739 --> 00:37:37,289
and an infinite number of faces.

667
00:37:37,340 --> 00:37:41,650
His head, I assure you, would
be your crowning achievement.

668
00:37:41,699 --> 00:37:45,929
Besides which, many of
us on this ship would be

669
00:37:45,980 --> 00:37:50,570
happy to see his career cut
off, as it were, at the neck.

670
00:37:50,619 --> 00:37:53,130
Proceed faster, or YOUR
head will be taken!

671
00:37:53,179 --> 00:37:55,210
I would give my head with gladness.

672
00:37:55,260 --> 00:37:58,530
This woman is the known
consort of the Doctor.

673
00:37:58,579 --> 00:38:01,099
Confirmation required. Uploading.

674
00:38:03,460 --> 00:38:06,449
Ooh. Ooh!

675
00:38:06,500 --> 00:38:10,449
Is River Song the consort of the
Time Lord known as the Doctor?

676
00:38:10,500 --> 00:38:11,889
Huh?

677
00:38:11,940 --> 00:38:13,530
I think so, yeah.

678
00:38:13,579 --> 00:38:17,289
Here, can I stay up for a bit?
It's really very whiffy down there.

679
00:38:17,340 --> 00:38:19,570
Aww!

680
00:38:19,619 --> 00:38:21,250
Oh, it's awful!

681
00:38:21,300 --> 00:38:25,219
So, where is the Doctor now?

682
00:38:26,300 --> 00:38:28,489
I haven't the faintest idea.

683
00:38:28,539 --> 00:38:31,329
- Is that credible?
- It's true.

684
00:38:31,380 --> 00:38:35,369
- You're the woman he loves.
- No, I'm not. - She's lying.

685
00:38:35,420 --> 00:38:39,980
The Doctor does not and has
never loved me. I'm not lying.

686
00:38:42,699 --> 00:38:47,130
- Confirmed. The life form is not lying.
- Impossible. This is a trick.

687
00:38:47,179 --> 00:38:50,730
- No, it isn't.
- My information is correct.

688
00:38:50,780 --> 00:38:53,250
You are the woman who loves the Doctor.

689
00:38:53,300 --> 00:38:54,969
Yes, I am. I've never denied it.

690
00:38:55,019 --> 00:38:57,289
But whoever said he loved me back?

691
00:38:57,340 --> 00:39:02,329
He's the Doctor, he doesn't go
around falling in love with people.

692
00:39:02,380 --> 00:39:06,250
And if you think he's anything
that small or that ordinary,

693
00:39:06,300 --> 00:39:09,900
then you haven't the first idea
of what you're dealing with.

694
00:39:11,219 --> 00:39:14,690
Your Majesty, I assure you,
she is the perfect bait.

695
00:39:14,739 --> 00:39:17,610
When this woman is in danger,
the Doctor will always come.

696
00:39:17,659 --> 00:39:20,210
Oh, you are a moron. No, he won't.

697
00:39:20,260 --> 00:39:23,210
- He's probably already here.
- No, he isn't, of course he isn't!

698
00:39:23,260 --> 00:39:26,449
- Possibly on this ship.
- Well, go on, scan it then.

699
00:39:26,500 --> 00:39:27,809
Go on, why don't you?

700
00:39:27,860 --> 00:39:30,969
- River...
- Two hearts, stupid clothes, you can't miss him.

701
00:39:31,019 --> 00:39:35,570
- River!
- Go on, scan the whole parsec! He's not here.

702
00:39:35,619 --> 00:39:38,769
God knows where he is right now,
but I promise you, he's doing

703
00:39:38,820 --> 00:39:41,929
whatever the hell he wants and
not giving a damn about me!

704
00:39:41,980 --> 00:39:43,809
And I'm just fine with that.

705
00:39:43,860 --> 00:39:45,610
- River...
- When you love the Doctor,

706
00:39:45,659 --> 00:39:47,730
it's like loving the stars themselves.

707
00:39:47,780 --> 00:39:50,650
You don't expect a
sunset to admire you back.

708
00:39:50,699 --> 00:39:53,809
And if I happen to find myself
in danger, let me tell you,

709
00:39:53,860 --> 00:39:57,889
the Doctor is not stupid
enough, or sentimental enough,

710
00:39:57,940 --> 00:40:00,489
and he is certainly not in love enough

711
00:40:00,539 --> 00:40:03,280
to find himself standing in it with me!

712
00:40:15,179 --> 00:40:16,849
Hello, sweetie.

713
00:40:22,780 --> 00:40:27,969
- You are so doing those roots.
- What, the roots of the sunset?

714
00:40:28,019 --> 00:40:31,369
- Don't you dare!
- I'll have to check with the stars themselves.

715
00:40:31,420 --> 00:40:34,530
Shut up! I was just keeping
them talking till it kicks off.

716
00:40:34,579 --> 00:40:37,210
- What is this conversation? Explain.
- You keep out of this.

717
00:40:37,260 --> 00:40:39,130
- We need to get to work.
- OK, what have you got?

718
00:40:39,179 --> 00:40:41,210
Four exits, two concealed,
one in the ceiling.

719
00:40:41,260 --> 00:40:43,329
- There's also one in the floor.
- No, I don't like it.

720
00:40:43,380 --> 00:40:45,329
- Too close to the engine ducts?
- A bit too tight.

721
00:40:45,380 --> 00:40:47,010
I hope you're not being personal.

722
00:40:47,059 --> 00:40:48,849
Excuse me, what are you talking about?

723
00:40:48,900 --> 00:40:50,530
Hush, Mummy and Daddy are busy.

724
00:40:50,579 --> 00:40:52,369
There we are.

725
00:40:52,420 --> 00:40:55,050
- Two o'clock, here we go.
- Cease this conversation.

726
00:40:55,099 --> 00:40:57,809
Darling, in the event of a
sudden meteor strike on the lower

727
00:40:57,860 --> 00:41:00,650
starboard decks, where would you
say is the safest place to stand?

728
00:41:00,699 --> 00:41:02,929
- Meteor strikes?
- Exactly here, I should think.

729
00:41:02,980 --> 00:41:05,889
- D'you know what that isn't? A coincidence.
- Your escape plan.

730
00:41:05,940 --> 00:41:08,809
- It's cheaper than a taxi.
- What meteor strike?

731
00:41:08,860 --> 00:41:11,409
'Alert. Meteor storm imminent.'

732
00:41:11,460 --> 00:41:14,650
- That meteor strike.
- How could you know?

733
00:41:14,699 --> 00:41:17,130
I'm an archaeologist from the future.

734
00:41:17,179 --> 00:41:18,900
I dug you up.

735
00:41:22,219 --> 00:41:24,300
See you in 400 years.

736
00:41:32,260 --> 00:41:35,690
I had this book. History's
Finest Exploding Restaurants.

737
00:41:35,739 --> 00:41:37,530
The best food for free. Skip the coffee.

738
00:41:37,579 --> 00:41:40,530
- What do you think, by the way?
- Of what? - My new body.

739
00:41:40,579 --> 00:41:42,969
I'll let you know. I've
only seen the face.

740
00:41:43,019 --> 00:41:45,610
How have you got a new one, by
the way? Aren't there rules?

741
00:41:45,659 --> 00:41:48,659
- A thing happened.
- I bet it probably did.

742
00:41:49,260 --> 00:41:54,369
'Starboard decks compromised.
Please abandon ship.'

743
00:41:54,420 --> 00:41:55,849
The diamond?

744
00:41:55,900 --> 00:41:59,659
- Good, aren't I?
- I'm not sure good's the word. - Better not be.

745
00:42:01,059 --> 00:42:04,090
- We need to get this ship stabilised. Where's the bridge?
- This way.

746
00:42:04,139 --> 00:42:06,139
'Please abandon ship.'

747
00:42:08,820 --> 00:42:10,489
'Please abandon ship.'

748
00:42:10,539 --> 00:42:12,969
- We also need to stop that.
- Toss for it.

749
00:42:13,019 --> 00:42:16,210
- I'll take the robot, you drive.
- OK.

750
00:42:16,260 --> 00:42:19,739
- Oh, don't stop for strangers.
- Look who's talking.

751
00:42:24,340 --> 00:42:27,250
- What's the point? It's over.
- I will take your head.

752
00:42:27,300 --> 00:42:30,530
What for? We're on a crashing
spaceship and I don't even know

753
00:42:30,579 --> 00:42:34,289
if I can save it. You just shot
your own king in your own face.

754
00:42:34,340 --> 00:42:37,130
- You'd get beheaded if you had one.
- I will take yours.

755
00:42:37,179 --> 00:42:39,579
King Hydroflax will live again.

756
00:42:46,940 --> 00:42:48,210
Do you know what you need?

757
00:42:48,260 --> 00:42:51,130
Do you know what any decent
headless king needs? Money.

758
00:42:51,179 --> 00:42:55,250
This connects every bank to
every other bank in this galaxy.

759
00:42:55,300 --> 00:42:59,409
Right here in my hand.
All the money you can eat.

760
00:42:59,460 --> 00:43:01,000
Demonstrate.

761
00:43:02,019 --> 00:43:03,619
With pleasure.

762
00:43:09,340 --> 00:43:12,929
Welcome to all the best
firewalls in the galaxy.

763
00:43:12,980 --> 00:43:14,809
Nothing is protected like money.

764
00:43:14,860 --> 00:43:17,889
Every stock market within a light
year is arguing in your head.

765
00:43:17,940 --> 00:43:19,570
I do not understand.

766
00:43:19,619 --> 00:43:22,210
Ha-ha! That's the way
it is for most people.

767
00:43:22,260 --> 00:43:24,929
Do not understand. Do not understand.

768
00:43:26,940 --> 00:43:29,650
- He had a bad day on the market.
- Do not understand.

769
00:43:29,699 --> 00:43:31,329
Do not understand.

770
00:43:31,380 --> 00:43:36,250
Sorry, I appreciate that wasn't very
funny, but I couldn't help saying it.

771
00:43:36,300 --> 00:43:39,300
Do not understand. Do not under...

772
00:43:40,380 --> 00:43:43,210
'Surface impact in two minutes.'

773
00:43:43,260 --> 00:43:45,210
Where's everyone else?

774
00:43:45,260 --> 00:43:48,849
- They ran for it. So should we.
- We need to get the nav com back online.

775
00:43:48,900 --> 00:43:51,900
- And re-route the thrusters.
- I'm trying.

776
00:43:52,980 --> 00:43:57,170
- So, King Hydroflax?
- Oh, how many times? I married the diamond.

777
00:43:57,219 --> 00:44:02,489
- So you say. - Elizabeth I. - Ramone.
- Marilyn Monroe. - Stephen Fry.

778
00:44:02,539 --> 00:44:04,739
- Cleopatra!
- Same thing.

779
00:44:07,739 --> 00:44:09,690
Hang on a minute.

780
00:44:09,739 --> 00:44:11,889
- I recognise that planet.
- Well, that's nice!

781
00:44:11,940 --> 00:44:14,809
Maybe they'll name the crater after us(!)

782
00:44:16,219 --> 00:44:17,960
That's Darillium!

783
00:44:20,860 --> 00:44:22,449
Always good to know where we're going.

784
00:44:22,500 --> 00:44:24,849
- Could you concentrate on your work, please?
- You know...

785
00:44:24,900 --> 00:44:25,900
the Singing Towers.

786
00:44:25,940 --> 00:44:28,059
Yes, I'll be sure to give
them a wave as we zoom past.

787
00:44:28,099 --> 00:44:30,369
You always say you're going
to take me there for dinner

788
00:44:30,420 --> 00:44:32,329
and then you always
cancel at the last minute.

789
00:44:32,380 --> 00:44:36,980
- I'd quite like to cancel this time too, if at all possible.
- Argh!

790
00:44:40,300 --> 00:44:42,530
What are you doing? That's
the internal teleport.

791
00:44:42,579 --> 00:44:43,610
Yes.

792
00:44:43,659 --> 00:44:47,769
- I can use the power cell to push the thrusters.
- Really? How?

793
00:44:47,820 --> 00:44:49,690
Hold this, quickly.

794
00:44:51,059 --> 00:44:52,849
Well, I don't see what good this will do.

795
00:44:52,900 --> 00:44:54,500
Sorry, River.

796
00:44:55,300 --> 00:44:58,699
- Crashing spaceships, that's my job.
- You...

797
00:45:01,380 --> 00:45:02,980
No, you don't!

798
00:45:06,739 --> 00:45:09,929
More power! You can do it, you can do it.

799
00:45:11,059 --> 00:45:14,619
No, River, no, no, no, no!

800
00:45:19,699 --> 00:45:22,489
- Get back in the TARDIS! This is my job!
- This is MY job!

801
00:45:22,539 --> 00:45:24,409
- I've been doing it longer.
- I do it better.

802
00:45:24,460 --> 00:45:27,130
River, not one person on this
ship, not one living thing,

803
00:45:27,179 --> 00:45:29,500
- is worth you.
- Or you.

804
00:45:30,699 --> 00:45:34,210
'Surface impact in ten, nine, eight...'

805
00:45:34,260 --> 00:45:36,130
- Teensy bit close.
- Yeah, sort of.

806
00:45:36,179 --> 00:45:38,530
- Darling, shall we pop back indoors?
- Yeah, good idea.

807
00:45:38,579 --> 00:45:41,739
'.. Four, three, two, one.'

808
00:46:07,619 --> 00:46:09,619
Indestructible as ever.

809
00:46:16,619 --> 00:46:18,619
Married the diamond(!)

810
00:47:08,340 --> 00:47:10,019
Hello? Sir...

811
00:47:12,420 --> 00:47:16,050
the ship, it came down, did you see it?
- Yes, I did.

812
00:47:16,099 --> 00:47:18,210
I've been searching for survivors.

813
00:47:18,260 --> 00:47:20,460
I doubt if you'd find any.
And I don't think any of them

814
00:47:20,500 --> 00:47:23,210
would be worth it, if that's a comfort.

815
00:47:23,260 --> 00:47:26,000
Brave of you to try, though. Well done.

816
00:47:26,739 --> 00:47:28,409
Thank you, sir.

817
00:47:31,780 --> 00:47:34,210
Those are the Singing Towers, aren't they?

818
00:47:34,260 --> 00:47:36,409
Yes, sir, but it's just the wind.

819
00:47:36,460 --> 00:47:38,929
The Singing Towers of Darillium.

820
00:47:39,980 --> 00:47:42,739
- Here we are at last.
- Sir?

821
00:47:44,179 --> 00:47:45,250
You know what?

822
00:47:45,300 --> 00:47:48,690
They should build a restaurant right
here, with a view of those towers.

823
00:47:48,739 --> 00:47:52,739
You could make a lot of money
that way. You should do that.

824
00:47:52,860 --> 00:47:55,329
You'd need a lot of
money to begin with, sir.

825
00:47:55,380 --> 00:47:56,610
The Halassi Androvar...

826
00:47:56,659 --> 00:48:00,300
I think you'll find that the
reward is pretty substantial.

827
00:48:07,860 --> 00:48:11,340
- Why would you give me this, sir?
- (Restaurant!)

828
00:48:30,300 --> 00:48:33,329
Excuse me, um, I'd like
a table on the balcony

829
00:48:33,380 --> 00:48:35,929
- with a view of the towers.
- I'm sorry, sir,

830
00:48:35,980 --> 00:48:39,289
the first available slot I have is
Christmas Day in four years' time.

831
00:48:39,340 --> 00:48:40,940
Not a problem.

832
00:48:52,219 --> 00:48:57,219
- Professor Song! The Doctor is waiting for you on the balcony.
- Oh.

833
00:48:59,699 --> 00:49:02,170
- Excellent.
- This way, ma'am.

834
00:49:02,820 --> 00:49:06,260
- Do we have a good table?
- The finest in all the galaxy, ma'am.

835
00:49:07,860 --> 00:49:09,010
Ah.

836
00:49:09,059 --> 00:49:10,730
Er, one moment.

837
00:49:19,219 --> 00:49:23,809
- Ramone?
- Professor Song. The Doctor will be with you in a moment.

838
00:49:23,860 --> 00:49:27,730
- What are you doing here?
- They pulled us from the wreckage, ma'am.

839
00:49:27,780 --> 00:49:30,980
Fixed us up. I've been
working here ever since.

840
00:49:31,699 --> 00:49:33,050
Don't worry.

841
00:49:33,099 --> 00:49:36,730
The nasty part's all gone...
got deleted in the merger.

842
00:49:36,780 --> 00:49:39,610
- What about Nardole?
- Oh, merry Christmas, ma'am.

843
00:49:39,659 --> 00:49:41,969
Yeah, good to see you again.

844
00:49:42,019 --> 00:49:45,170
- Merry Christmas, Nardole!
- Sorry I'm off duty.

845
00:49:45,219 --> 00:49:47,010
I'm just having some me time.

846
00:49:47,059 --> 00:49:51,369
- I imagine that must be quite a challenge.
- Yes, ma'am.

847
00:49:53,019 --> 00:49:54,659
So, Ramone...

848
00:49:56,619 --> 00:49:58,090
you have a metal body now.

849
00:49:58,139 --> 00:49:59,739
Down, girl!

850
00:50:02,820 --> 00:50:06,539
- Now, that, my dear, IS a suit.
- Happy Christmas.

851
00:50:07,820 --> 00:50:09,159
Really?

852
00:50:10,019 --> 00:50:13,519
I don't think you've ever
given me a present before.

853
00:50:18,219 --> 00:50:20,650
It's a sonic screwdriver! How lovely!

854
00:50:20,699 --> 00:50:22,130
When I saw the sonic trowel,

855
00:50:22,179 --> 00:50:25,280
I thought it was just
embarrassing, but, look.

856
00:50:27,099 --> 00:50:28,699
Oh, thank you.

857
00:50:32,099 --> 00:50:34,369
You look, er, amazing.

858
00:50:34,420 --> 00:50:38,210
Doctor, you have no idea
whether I look amazing or not.

859
00:50:38,260 --> 00:50:41,329
- Well, you've moved your hair about, haven't you?
- Well done.

860
00:50:41,380 --> 00:50:45,179
- It's very sweet of you to try.
- So what do you think?

861
00:50:48,860 --> 00:50:50,730
The Singing Towers.

862
00:51:06,099 --> 00:51:07,570
The music.

863
00:51:18,300 --> 00:51:19,900
Listen to it.

864
00:51:23,699 --> 00:51:25,369
Are you crying?

865
00:51:26,460 --> 00:51:27,489
No.

866
00:51:27,539 --> 00:51:29,139
Just the wind.

867
00:51:30,139 --> 00:51:32,480
Nothing's ever just the wind.

868
00:51:32,980 --> 00:51:34,119
No?

869
00:51:35,619 --> 00:51:37,650
It blows through the cave system

870
00:51:37,699 --> 00:51:40,440
and harmonises with the crystal layer.

871
00:51:41,539 --> 00:51:43,280
Why are you sad?

872
00:51:44,340 --> 00:51:46,079
Why are YOU sad?

873
00:51:47,139 --> 00:51:49,530
I told you, my diary's nearly full.

874
00:51:49,579 --> 00:51:51,019
I worry.

875
00:51:52,219 --> 00:51:53,820
Please don't.

876
00:51:59,019 --> 00:52:02,210
- There are stories about us, you know.
- Oh, I dread to think.

877
00:52:02,260 --> 00:52:05,329
- I look them up sometimes.
- You really shouldn't do that.

878
00:52:05,380 --> 00:52:07,940
Some of them suggest that...

879
00:52:09,619 --> 00:52:11,730
the very last night we spend together

880
00:52:11,780 --> 00:52:14,519
is at the Singing Towers of Darillium.

881
00:52:16,139 --> 00:52:18,610
That wouldn't be true, would it?

882
00:52:21,340 --> 00:52:22,739
Spoilers.

883
00:52:26,940 --> 00:52:30,329
Well, that would explain why
you kept cancelling coming here.

884
00:52:30,380 --> 00:52:33,449
- Do you remember that time...
- River, stop. - .. When there were two of you...

885
00:52:33,500 --> 00:52:36,289
- Don't. - .. Because I want you to
know that if this is the last night,

886
00:52:36,340 --> 00:52:37,730
I expect you to find a way round it.

887
00:52:37,780 --> 00:52:40,119
Not everything can be avoided.

888
00:52:41,900 --> 00:52:43,440
Not forever.

889
00:52:44,019 --> 00:52:45,699
But you're you.

890
00:52:47,099 --> 00:52:49,690
There's always a loophole,
you wait until the last minute

891
00:52:49,739 --> 00:52:52,090
- and then you spring it on me.
- Every night is the last night

892
00:52:52,139 --> 00:52:55,090
- for something, every Christmas is the last Christmas...
- But you will.

893
00:52:55,139 --> 00:52:57,769
You'll wait until I've given
up hope, all will be lost,

894
00:52:57,820 --> 00:52:59,929
and you'll do that smug little smile

895
00:52:59,980 --> 00:53:02,090
and then you'll save the
day... you always do.

896
00:53:02,139 --> 00:53:04,210
No, I don't, not always.

897
00:53:06,420 --> 00:53:09,010
Times end, River, because they have to.

898
00:53:09,059 --> 00:53:11,570
Because there's no such
thing as happy ever after.

899
00:53:11,619 --> 00:53:14,780
It's just a lie we tell ourselves
because the truth is so hard.

900
00:53:15,739 --> 00:53:17,340
No, Doctor...

901
00:53:18,619 --> 00:53:20,360
you're wrong.

902
00:53:20,980 --> 00:53:23,719
Happy ever after doesn't mean forever.

903
00:53:25,019 --> 00:53:27,179
It just means time...

904
00:53:28,940 --> 00:53:30,679
a little time.

905
00:53:33,460 --> 00:53:36,860
But that's not the sort of thing
you could ever understand, is it?

906
00:53:38,940 --> 00:53:40,139
Mmm.

907
00:53:41,860 --> 00:53:45,780
- What do you think of the towers?
- I love them.

908
00:53:47,139 --> 00:53:50,340
- Then why are you ignoring them?
- They're ignoring me.

909
00:53:51,300 --> 00:53:55,809
But then... you can't expect
a monolith to love you back.

910
00:53:55,860 --> 00:53:57,460
No, you can't.

911
00:54:00,099 --> 00:54:02,369
They've been there for millions of years,

912
00:54:02,420 --> 00:54:06,570
through storms and floods
and wars and... time.

913
00:54:06,619 --> 00:54:10,010
Nobody really understands
where the music comes from.

914
00:54:10,059 --> 00:54:12,530
It's probably something to
do with the precise positions,

915
00:54:12,579 --> 00:54:14,650
the distance between both towers.

916
00:54:14,699 --> 00:54:16,409
Even the locals aren't sure.

917
00:54:16,460 --> 00:54:18,210
All anyone will ever tell you is

918
00:54:18,260 --> 00:54:21,500
that when the wind stands fair
and the night is perfect...

919
00:54:22,699 --> 00:54:25,039
when you least expect it...

920
00:54:26,179 --> 00:54:27,920
but always...

921
00:54:29,300 --> 00:54:31,699
when you need it the most...

922
00:54:37,659 --> 00:54:39,619
there is a song.

923
00:54:47,820 --> 00:54:49,019
So...

924
00:54:50,780 --> 00:54:53,489
assuming tonight is all we have left...

925
00:54:53,539 --> 00:54:56,280
- I didn't say that.
- .. how long...

926
00:54:57,820 --> 00:55:00,099
is a night on Darillium?

927
00:55:03,260 --> 00:55:04,900
24 years.

928
00:55:13,019 --> 00:55:14,619
I hate you.

929
00:55:17,539 --> 00:55:18,820
No, you don't.
